- Are you a young graduate

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.460
who is applying for the first job?

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.530
Are you a young professional

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.920
who is looking to transition careers?

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:07.753
Surely,

00:00:07.753 --> 00:00:09.760
one thing that would be
very important to succeed

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.410
is a strong CV.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.580
When I applied to the
consulting firm McKinsey,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.440
back in the days

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.170
I faced the same challenge.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.003
So in this video,

00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:20.350
I wanna share some of my
knowledge by reviewing your CVs.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.983
So a couple of days ago on my Instagram,

00:00:21.983 --> 00:00:24.870
I asked you to submit some CVs to me,

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.610
for me to potentially review them.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.300
If you want to have your CV included

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.350
in potential future videos like this,

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.510
follow me on Instagram.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.910
This is where I most likely
will talk about this again.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.740
Before we start diving into the CVs,

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.640
a couple of preliminary remarks,

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.473
first of all,

00:00:38.473 --> 00:00:41.530
all of these things are of
course just my humble opinions,

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.940
my humble experiences,

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.180
surely the topic of how
a strong CV looks like

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.013
is a topic

00:00:46.013 --> 00:00:48.380
where many people have
many differing opinions on,

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.370
but feel free to challenge
me also in the comments.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.270
If you have another view

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.650
on any of the points that I'm raising.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.290
So welcome to another coffee
break here on my channel,

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.123
Firm Learning,

00:00:56.123 --> 00:00:57.070
my name is Heinrich

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.650
and on my channel I want to help you

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.280
to become successful in the
first years of your career.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.113
In addition,

00:01:02.113 --> 00:01:04.580
also for both the CV and
a cover letter template

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.910
for you as a download,

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:09.450
these were the very same
templates that I used myself,

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.830
when I successfully applied
to the consulting firm,

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:13.090
McKinsey, back in the days.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.770
You'll find a link to them
in the video description,

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.330
so feel free to check them out.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.690
So let's start looking
at this first CV here

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.710
and let just go by a
very first impression.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:21.780
So just looking at this,

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:23.100
how does this seem?

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.100
Does this seem professional
and good or not?

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.480
And I'd say this is not very bad.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.730
I mean, it's not, not terrible,

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.310
but there's surely some
things that you could improve.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.350
So let's look just at a couple of things

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.910
that I think are not really on point,

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.010
not really ideal here.

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:38.410
And for us, let's start
with some alignment points.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.690
I'm just zooming in here.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:40.890
Let's go up here.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.530
We see that here that all kind
of different levels are used

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:45.440
when things start, right?

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.050
So here you have a level of text

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.650
where this level, it starts,

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.650
this here is a bit dented
further to the right.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.940
This line here is even a bit
further left than this stuff.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.740
This here is even further left.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:00.070
So you see all different
types of layout levels.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.540
So where elements start.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:02.373
All right, next,

00:02:02.373 --> 00:02:04.450
let's talk a bit more about the content,

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:08.583
for instance about an
introductory text like this.

00:02:08.583 --> 00:02:10.180
It's actually many CVs that I received,

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.940
I saw people including
a little intro text here

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:13.773
in the beginning,

00:02:13.773 --> 00:02:15.820
and here, I'm not saying
this is a deal breaker.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.470
How this alone we get you rejected,

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.440
but let's just try to put ourselves

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.810
into the shoes of a person who reads CV's.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.160
You will have big stack of CV's,

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.130
a big stack of paper on your desk.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:28.820
You would just go one after the other.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.910
We try to skim the CV for some keywords,

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:33.610
for the key things that you did.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:34.670
Where did you work?

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:35.540
Where did you study?

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.373
What are your grades?

00:02:36.373 --> 00:02:37.720
What are your responsibilities?

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.350
I would argue that these people

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:41.070
really not even care to bother,

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:44.730
to start reading a big
paragraph of text like this.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.665
So Max is a strategy
and consulting manager,

00:02:47.665 --> 00:02:51.140
and he's aligned to the company,
Capital Markets Practice.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.210
He has a professional understanding
of the financial sector,

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.400
blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.368
I mean,

00:02:56.368 --> 00:02:57.430
these are things that
we would directly see

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.840
if you read it right
here, senior consultant.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:00.673
What did you do?

00:03:00.673 --> 00:03:01.620
Security settlement.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.453
Okay. Got it.

00:03:02.453 --> 00:03:03.377
Right.

00:03:03.377 --> 00:03:04.440
So no need for any explanations like this.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.540
Next, let's talk about a
picture here in the top, right?

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.630
This is also a question
that I get quite frequently.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.380
So are you supposed to include
a picture in the CV or not?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.060
And here I'd say it really depends

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.160
probably most on the
region where you apply to.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.620
So I'd argue more on the
Anglosaxon countries,

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.740
so UK also the US and so on,

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.730
I'd say it's rather
unusual to include it for,

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.380
of course, discrimination reasons.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.380
You don't want CVs to be assessed

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:29.240
based on the looks of
a person, for instance.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.220
in countries like Germany,

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.760
I would claim that it is
still very common to have a

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:33.990
picture on your CV.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.870
So probably I would also still do it

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.240
in a country like Germany,

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.710
though, if you apply, for instance,

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.230
via are online form,

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:42.730
often that online forms
have specific fields

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.340
where you can upload a picture.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.660
So if you did already upload
a picture to such a form,

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.140
then I'd say you also don't
need the picture on the CV.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:49.973
Personally,

00:03:49.973 --> 00:03:52.680
on my standard CV, don't have
a picture included of course,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.640
with the nice one page format

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.830
that I would recommend
you to use in general,

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.180
a picture takes a lot of space.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.750
Often doesn't integrate
that nicely in the layout.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:01.583
So if you can,

00:04:01.583 --> 00:04:03.600
I'll probably try to get
away with not including it

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.433
on the CV,

00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:06.080
but in some reasons it's
truly not a problem.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.097
Next, let's talk about,

00:04:07.097 --> 00:04:09.130
there's a very general
layout here of the CV

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:12.080
where you have here the key
content side on the left,

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.490
and then this additional
bar here on the right

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.980
and actually several CVs that you sent me

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.680
had variations of this layout.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:20.202
In my humble perspective on is

00:04:20.202 --> 00:04:22.920
that I would probably rather
not go for these layouts.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.490
So surely if you apply
to a marketing agency

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:28.060
or maybe another very creative job, sure.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.770
Be creative, do some fancy,

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.104
maybe also build an
Orthodox stuff on your CV,

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:33.160
I trust there it's okay.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.540
But especially if you apply to
more conservative industries

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.560
like consulting or like banking,

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:40.900
surely you will not get
invited to an interview

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.720
because of the way how
you lay outed your CV.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.980
This is just not the way
of thinking about this.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.200
The best case scenario is

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.890
the people who just not care
that use the layout like this.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.670
But of course the worst case scenarios

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.880
that this will rub people the wrong way,

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:54.750
people might feel like,

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.320
ah, maybe you didn't do your research.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.010
You didn't know how a typical CV layout

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:00.470
for these industries look like.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.303
And surely

00:05:01.303 --> 00:05:02.630
this is not the impression
that you want to leave.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:04.770
And I'd argue also from
a functional perspective,

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.440
layouts like this are not very effective.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:08.600
Let's just see how much
space is wasted here

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.980
with the personal info.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:11.780
The personal info you can usually include

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.150
just in one line in the very
head of your one page CV.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.900
You will later see a
couple of other examples

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:17.890
of people did that.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.500
And same thing here for the languages.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.170
I mean, this takes so much space.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.570
You can just write this in one simple line

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:24.880
and let's not even get me started here

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.840
on all these dots to indicate
your language proficiency.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:28.970
Because indeed what we do see

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.030
is that actually the font size
here of the volume of the CV

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.270
is very small.

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.740
This is a very small font size.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:36.573
And yes,

00:05:36.573 --> 00:05:37.760
I gather that on one page of CVs,

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.170
often you have lots of texts

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.600
and often the font size
cannot be too large,

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.360
but this is very small, right?

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.270
And you would have all
these other opportunities

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:46.920
to make more space for the text,

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.240
increase the font size.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.270
And also in general,

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.820
at least in the body of your CV,

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:54.030
I would recommend you to
always use the same font size.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:55.940
It always looks a bit unclean,

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.320
not very polished

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.940
if you have fewer texts
with a larger font size,

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:01.120
then here, it gets smaller,

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.690
this is larger again,

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:04.260
it doesn't just look very clean,

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.093
very polished.

00:06:05.093 --> 00:06:07.740
So rather go for the same
font size whenever possible.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.200
Let's move to the second CV.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.033
And by the way,

00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:11.370
I will try all the different CVs

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.850
to highlight different things, right?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.730
So only cause I don't point out again,

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.840
the things that I maybe
pointed out on prior CV,

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.950
of course, they're still
very much all true,

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.020
but let's just continue here.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.850
And very first impression,

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:23.560
again, maybe think about
this for yourself, right?

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.480
What is the very first
impression that you have?

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:27.980
And I'd say it's rather good.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:28.813
I like it.

00:06:28.813 --> 00:06:30.420
I think it's very clear,
very well organized.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.040
The layout seems nice
and clean and principal,

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:33.873
I like it here.

00:06:33.873 --> 00:06:35.090
Here we also see some of these

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.180
a bit more modern layout elements,

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.420
like these icons here to
indicate your address,

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.730
the phone and so on,

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:43.040
this blue border around your picture,

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.410
this light gray or these blue bars here

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:47.023
to indicate a new subsection.

00:06:47.023 --> 00:06:47.950
I mean, I don't know.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:50.095
So surely this won't get you rejected,

00:06:50.095 --> 00:06:51.660
personally I also think it looks good.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:52.950
Here's still probably myself,

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.970
if I would write a CV for me,

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.920
I would still go for the
very conservative style

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.670
without all these things included.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.420
The thing that probably bothers me most

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:02.900
is just the length.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.460
And this is just a lot of
content, two full pages.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:07.300
And let's also not forget

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.610
that this person is still a student.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.130
And I know that the general rule is

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.980
that up to two pages is okay.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:14.960
I think more than two pages is really bad.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:16.080
You should not do it,

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.270
but I would still
recommend you to go for the

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:19.920
one pager layout.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.250
Every single CV out there

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.470
you can condense to one pager layout.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:26.470
Even if you have 30, 40
years of work experience,

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.930
it's always possible to
bring it to one page.

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:31.720
Of course, what this means
is that you need to focus.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.470
You maybe need to cut out some things

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.600
which are not the strongest
things you want to talk about,

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.300
or really reduce them to a minimum.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:38.670
But trust that everybody already

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:40.820
was in the position to review CVs.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.300
It's almost much nicer to have one page

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:45.650
just instead of always
needing to go back and forth

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.970
across different pages.

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:48.270
And also one page in general

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:51.310
helps you much more to really
focus on your awesomeness.

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:53.030
So ideally the impression
that you want to create

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.570
is that someone reads your CV

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.220
and every single line, right?

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:57.650
Every single line just reads.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:58.870
Wow, this is crazy.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.900
Impressive, impressive, awesome.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:01.740
Never seen this.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:02.940
This is incredible.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.270
But if you drag out the
content over two pages,

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:07.640
usually you don't have enough
things to really fill it

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:09.080
with that much awesomeness.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.260
Then the awesome points,

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.490
really just get lost,

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:12.727
the more mediocre points.

00:08:12.727 --> 00:08:14.770
And this is just not the first impression

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:15.603
that you want to give.

00:08:15.603 --> 00:08:16.750
So let's just look at that.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.080
What are the things that maybe
you would want to cut out?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.890
Maybe you don't want
to focus on that much.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.090
And here, if you read it surely

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:25.290
the big household names like
BMW, Allanson and so on,

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.940
these surely are the things
you do wanna focus on,

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.474
but then you also read
things like Neurodynamics,

00:08:30.474 --> 00:08:33.680
ABCA strategy consultants and so on.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:34.687
And if as a student,

00:08:34.687 --> 00:08:36.500
you already have these
very strong internships

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.670
at BMW, Allanson and so on.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.050
You think someone will really care

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.930
that you've worked at Neurodynamics

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.630
or CA Strategy Consultants.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:44.463
And again,

00:08:44.463 --> 00:08:45.790
don't want to come off
here as condescending.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:46.970
I just don't know these firms.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.650
Maybe these are very great firms,

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:50.170
some hidden champions in a very niche,

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.900
but I'd argue the general HR content

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:52.737
will just not know them.

00:08:52.737 --> 00:08:54.460
And just also one thing to understand is

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:57.330
that you don't need to list
every single work experience,

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.700
every single internship
that you ever completed

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.533
throughout your life.

00:09:00.533 --> 00:09:02.350
So probably at the point
