the structure of the CV
is very good and clean.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:42.980
So you start with education,

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:44.750
professional experiences,

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:45.840
leadership and awards,

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:47.370
volunteer experience.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.203
Very good,

00:17:48.203 --> 00:17:49.036
very clear,

00:17:49.036 --> 00:17:49.869
very well done.

00:17:49.869 --> 00:17:51.640
The one thing that maybe
is a little bit unorthodox

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:52.630
just with these a bit more

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.000
like modern design elements

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.500
are these points that were included here,

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:57.333
but why not?

00:17:57.333 --> 00:17:59.090
I mean, again, surely
this won't be a problem.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:01.160
One little, I guess error is here.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.780
The spacing between the points, right?

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:04.880
So here, apparently a space is missing.

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:06.600
Whereas here we have spaces,

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.140
here again, the space is missing,

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:09.570
here again a spaces missing,

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:11.360
similar, I think here
also with the dashes.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.112
So here there are spaces
between the dashes,

00:18:14.112 --> 00:18:15.290
here there are no spaces
between the dashes.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:18.070
Here, again inconsistencies
with the EM and EN dashes.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:20.090
So the longer and the shorter dash,

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:22.570
again, maybe I'm just too super
critical about these things,

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:24.660
but these are things when I look at CVs,

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.110
for whatever reason, they
just directly jump in my eye.

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:29.030
I just cannot help but
notice these things.

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:30.430
And of course the underlying reasoning,

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:32.320
why these things maybe do matter is that

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.230
if you work for instance
in professional services,

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:36.230
you create documents for your clients.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:38.440
You will for sure get feedback
on points like this, right?

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:39.907
So if in your client documents,

00:18:39.907 --> 00:18:43.000
you just mess up only these
small layout inconsistencies.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:43.833
I mean,

00:18:43.833 --> 00:18:45.000
these are things that
you will get feedback on

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.520
from a project lead, for
your team lead and so on.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.920
And of course the logic is that,

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:49.930
you know, this is your CV.

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:53.670
So this is a document where you
surely invested lots of time

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:54.950
to really get it right

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.720
to the smallest amount of detail, right?

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:57.650
I mean, the impression of course,

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:59.250
that this creates is that maybe you lack

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:00.530
the attention of detail

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:03.080
and if you cannot even
get such a document right,

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:05.180
how are you expected to
get these things right

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:06.660
if it's already, you know, late at night,

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.890
you are under lots of pressure

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:09.260
in a short amount of time.

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:11.300
You need to create a
significant amount of documents.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:12.416
I mean,

00:19:12.416 --> 00:19:13.700
this is just the reasoning
that an HR professional

00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:15.060
might have in his or her head

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:16.670
when just looking at things like that

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:17.880
and then making comments on that.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:18.713
But overall,

00:19:18.713 --> 00:19:19.546
I must say I do like it,

00:19:19.546 --> 00:19:21.230
also notice to here how
the bullets are written,

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:22.063
for instance,

00:19:22.063 --> 00:19:25.080
this person rights increased
acetic acid product sales

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:28.160
by 50% by revitalizing
distributor portfolio

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.240
and adding to customer
base and so on, so forth.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.483
So you really focus on the impact here.

00:19:31.483 --> 00:19:32.900
Here also the next one

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:37.090
contributed towards annual
saving of over 80,000 Euro

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:40.120
written something that
reduced OPEX cost by 12%

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:42.550
saving 50,000 Euro and so on and so forth.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:45.700
So really always pushing
for the measurable impact.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.800
This is the style that you want to go for.

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:49.860
Just my little other layout style is,

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:50.693
I mean, first of all,

00:19:50.693 --> 00:19:53.340
I really this idea of
bolding things like that,

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:55.480
I think this really helps guide the eye

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:56.870
to the most important words,

00:19:56.870 --> 00:19:58.640
to the things that you
really wanna focus on.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.290
But then I would argue if you do this,

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:02.500
try to have then one bolded thing

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:03.900
in all of the bullet points.

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:04.733
So for instance,

00:20:04.733 --> 00:20:06.850
here is also actually
quite big bullet point

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.420
without any bolded elements.

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:09.400
Here I would also argue

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:11.850
that I think two lines
of text for one bullet

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:13.230
usually are enough.

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:15.460
So rather condense a bullet of three lines

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.060
a bit further to two lines.

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:19.120
This just looks a little bit cleaner.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:19.953
Also,

00:20:19.953 --> 00:20:21.220
if then all the other
bullets are two lines

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:22.053
as we have it here

00:20:22.053 --> 00:20:24.130
than if you have suddenly
a bullet of three lines,

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.330
the somewhat sticks out,

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:26.810
probably not really necessary,

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:27.790
rather cut it down.

00:20:27.790 --> 00:20:28.623
And then of course,

00:20:28.623 --> 00:20:30.850
if you do have a nice CV like
that with all this content,

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:31.990
probably what I would think about

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:33.030
whether that you wouldn't want to give

00:20:33.030 --> 00:20:35.510
a little bit more space to
the volunteering experience.

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:36.343
I mean,

00:20:36.343 --> 00:20:39.450
this can be a little nice
additional touch on what you did

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:41.950
makes you seem to be a bit
more of a rounded character,

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:42.883
right?

00:20:42.883 --> 00:20:44.090
Not a person just lives for a CV,

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.930
not only a person lives
for his or her education,

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.760
GPA and work experience.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.350
If you were writing for social causes,

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.940
I trust you raised money maybe, right.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:53.120
For social cause.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.270
So why don't talk about that?

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.530
How much money you raised,

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:57.030
what your leadership position was

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:58.320
and bringing this to life,

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.620
making sure that this
happened last but not least,

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.390
just because we haven't talked
about it in that much detail,

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:06.510
I'd argue probably most
regions it's very customary.

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:07.560
So in your education section,

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:09.810
when you talk about your degrees,

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:12.500
that you'll also include your GPA.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:13.333
Again,

00:21:13.333 --> 00:21:15.890
I understand that university
systems are a bit different,

00:21:15.890 --> 00:21:18.460
but if you received any
type of numeric GPA,

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:21.240
I would recommend you to
also included here on the CV.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:23.960
Sometimes people ask me when
my GPA wasn't that strong,

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:25.240
should I still include it?

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:27.140
Even if it wasn't that strong?

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:29.140
And I'd say yes, because at least myself,

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.910
usually whenever I see a CV without GPA,

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:35.600
I just assume that the person
doesn't have such a great GPA,

00:21:35.600 --> 00:21:36.513
right?

00:21:36.513 --> 00:21:38.120
Because otherwise the person
would show it on the CV.

00:21:38.120 --> 00:21:39.940
And then it's always just an annoyance

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:42.180
to needing to look at the
university transcripts

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:44.110
maybe that the person
hopefully then attached,

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.620
just look through all the
documents to pull out the GPAs

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.050
that the person actually has,

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.030
this is just annoying,

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.160
a waste of time,

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.650
be transparent, include them.

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:54.097
And of course, ideally
what always also helps.

00:21:54.097 --> 00:21:54.930
And you probably,

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:57.080
I would only include it if
really these numbers are good,

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.670
but if you have a good
also percentage rank.

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.380
So if you can show that you
are part of the top five,

00:22:02.380 --> 00:22:05.660
top 10, maybe top 15% of your class,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:07.850
I would surely include this
year in the CV as well.

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:08.683
Because of course,

00:22:08.683 --> 00:22:10.230
this helps also the HR professional,

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:12.160
just to understand and contextualize

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:13.630
the GPA a little better,

00:22:13.630 --> 00:22:15.735
especially maybe if you're
applying for university,

00:22:15.735 --> 00:22:18.050
maybe isn't one of the big target schools

00:22:18.050 --> 00:22:20.840
where it's a bit less clear
on what the GPA really means,

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:22.890
whether this is a good reside or not.

